sequenceDiagram
    actor Rep as Reporter
    participant REP as ModerationEndpoints
    participant RS as ReportService
    participant DB as AppDbContext / PostgreSQL
    actor Mod as Community Moderator
    participant MAS as ModerationActionService
    participant ND as NotificationDispatcher

    Rep->>REP: POST /api/posts/{id}/reports {category, reason}
    REP->>RS: CreateAsync(Post, id, reporterId, category, reason)
    RS->>DB: INSERT Report (Status = Open)

    Mod->>REP: GET /api/communities/{name}/mod/reports
    REP->>REP: AuthorizeAsync(user, community, "CommunityModerator")
    REP->>RS: list open reports for this community

    Mod->>REP: POST /api/communities/{name}/mod/reports/{id}/resolve {outcome}
    REP->>RS: GetCommunityIdForReportAsync(report) — re-verify ownership

    alt report belongs to a different community
        RS-->>REP: mismatch
        REP-->>Mod: 404
    else matches this community
        REP->>RS: ResolveAsync(report, communityId, modId, outcome)
        RS->>DB: UPDATE Report.Status = ActionTaken | Dismissed
        opt outcome = ActionTaken
            RS->>MAS: RecordReportResolutionAsync(...)
            MAS->>DB: INSERT ModerationAction (ReportResolve)
        end
        Note over Mod,MAS: Resolving is just the audit trail —<br/>actual remediation is a separate explicit call below
    end

    Mod->>REP: POST /api/posts/{id}/mod/remove
    REP->>MAS: RemoveAsync(postId, modId, reason)
    MAS->>DB: UPDATE Post.IsRemoved = true
    MAS->>DB: INSERT ModerationAction (Remove)
    MAS->>ND: DispatchAsync(authorId, ModAction, ...)

    Mod->>REP: POST /api/communities/{name}/mod/bans {username, reason}
    REP->>MAS: BanAsync(communityId, targetUserId, modId, reason)
    MAS->>DB: INSERT CommunityBan
    MAS->>DB: INSERT ModerationAction (Ban, CommunityId set)
    MAS->>ND: notify target
